Package: eva-dkms
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms (>= 2.8.3)
Description: EVA (CVP) DKMS kernel driver
 EVA is the dedicated computer-vision accelerator block on Snapdragon platforms.
 This package contains the DKMS source for the msm-eva kernel driver, built and
 installed against the currently running kernel by DKMS.
 .
 The driver exposes the EVA/CVP hardware queue interface (HFI) to
 userspace, manages EVA firmware load, power/clock/bus scaling, IOMMU
 context banks, and buffer/session lifecycle for camera and vision
 workloads offloaded to the EVA core.

Package: eva-linux-dev
Architecture: arm64
Provides: eva-uapi-dev
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: EVA (CVP) Linux kernel headers (UAPI)
 EVA (Enhanced Vision Accelerator, exposed to the kernel as CVP) is the
 dedicated computer-vision accelerator block on Snapdragon platforms.
 .
 This package provides the Linux kernel headers specifically needed to
 build userspace libraries and applications for EVA (UAPI).
